Q1. What is Spring Testing?

Interview Ready Answer

Spring Testing is used to test Spring Boot applications using JUnit
and Mockito.

It supports Unit Testing, Integration Testing, and testing different
layers of a Spring Boot application such as Controllers, Services,
and Repositories.

Key Points

• Used for testing Spring Boot applications.
• Uses JUnit and Mockito.
• Supports Unit Testing.
• Supports Integration Testing.
• Tests different application layers.

======================================================================

Q2. What is @SpringBootTest?

Interview Ready Answer

@SpringBootTest is a Spring Boot annotation used for Integration
Testing.

It loads the complete Spring Application Context so that all layers
of the application work together during testing.

Purpose

• Loads complete Spring Context.
• Used for Integration Testing.
• Tests the entire application.

======================================================================

Q3. What is @WebMvcTest?

Interview Ready Answer

@WebMvcTest is used to test only the Controller layer of a Spring Boot
application.

It does not load the complete Spring Application Context, making the
tests faster.

Purpose

• Tests Controller only.
• Verifies REST endpoints.
• Returns HTTP request/response.
• Faster than @SpringBootTest.

======================================================================

Q4. What is @DataJpaTest?

Interview Ready Answer

@DataJpaTest is used to test only the Repository layer.

It verifies database operations such as Save, Update, Delete and Find.
Spring Boot usually uses an in-memory H2 database during these tests.

Purpose

• Tests Repository layer.
• Verifies CRUD operations.
• Uses H2 in-memory database.
• Faster Repository testing.

======================================================================

Q5. Why are Repositories mocked during Service Testing?

Interview Ready Answer

Repositories are mocked so that only the Service layer's business
logic is tested.

This avoids connecting to a real database and makes Unit Tests
faster, isolated, and reliable.

Advantages

• No real database required.
• Faster execution.
• Tests only business logic.
• Independent Unit Testing.

======================================================================

Q6. What is @MockBean?

Interview Ready Answer

@MockBean is a Spring Boot testing annotation used to replace a real
Spring Bean with a Mock Bean inside the Spring Application Context.

It prevents real external dependencies from being called during
testing.

======================================================================

Q7. Difference between @SpringBootTest, @WebMvcTest and @DataJpaTest.

Interview Ready Answer

@SpringBootTest

• Loads complete Spring Application Context.
• Used for Integration Testing.
• Tests the complete application.

------------------------------------------------------------

@WebMvcTest

• Tests only Controller layer.
• Does not load complete application.
• Used for REST API testing.

------------------------------------------------------------

@DataJpaTest

• Tests only Repository layer.
• Verifies CRUD operations.
• Uses H2 in-memory database.

======================================================================

Q8. Difference between @Mock and @MockBean.

Interview Ready Answer

@Mock

• Mockito annotation.
• Creates a mock object.
• Used in Unit Testing.
• Does not load Spring Context.

------------------------------------------------------------

@MockBean

• Spring Boot annotation.
• Creates a Mock Spring Bean.
• Replaces a real bean inside Spring Context.
• Used in Spring Boot Testing.

